      "post_subject": "Nautilus Shell",
      "content_md": "The Nautilus organism lives in the last chamber. As it grows larger it needs larger \"digs\" so each chamber represents a \"new\" and larger home. There is a hole that goes through the center of each plate that separates one chamber from the next and a slender portion of the Nautilus extends through the holes back to the smallest chamber. As far as I know, the Nautilus hasn't changed much in several hundred million years. Amazing!",
